// Packet 0810 extends the existing SemIndex owner; every body in this window
// already lives in the canonical shared walker below. No aliases or duplicate
// AST walkers are introduced. These anchors map the Rust items to those bodies.

// normalize_definition -> Structure.jet:339 semindex_normalize_definition. Preserves
// quoted text/escaped scalars; drops // comments and outside whitespace.
// structural_nodes_from_parsed -> Structure.jet:375 semindex_structural_nodes_from_parsed.
// Sorts copied block spans and traverses the loaded Program using the same
// semindex_collect_item; an empty parsed name ledger is intentional Rust behavior.
// add_breadcrumb_hints -> Structure.jet:385–410 semindex_breadcrumb_label and
// semindex_add_breadcrumb_hints. Remote methods filter by owner/origin, then sort by
// origin label/name/module/start and retain the exact + signature [path:span]. build_index
// -> Structure.jet:415 semindex_build_index, with the checked registration/source/effect
// inputs forwarded to Finalize.semindex_build_symbol_db.

// collect_item -> Items.jet:81–222 semindex_collect_item plus ItemFacts.jet:17–166
// semindex_collect_item_facts/semindex_extern_callable_kind. Items owns
// record/push/state references/pop; its Func/Struct/Enum/Trait/Tag/Impl arms
// retain params, public labels, policies, bypasses, fields, states, payload types,
// member origins, trait requirements and method caller/slot context. Remaining
// arms are ItemFacts' MarkerDecl/FactDecl/Const/Test/ExternRust/Module/
// CodeModule/Distinct/TypeAlias/UnitFamily/ProtocolDecl/UserDerive/TemplateLoop/
// GenericModule/ModuleAlias. CodeModule restores its prior scope; derive loops
// inspect nested sources without inventing recursive expansion. EffectDecl,
// CModule, ErrorConv and Migration are original deliberate no-index arms.
// ExternRust indexes the wrapper contract only, marks failure/generic facts
// unavailable at Typed, and never treats rust_path as a source location.
// hover_for_fn -> ItemFacts.jet:170 semindex_hover_for_fn. Preserves public label
// head, / and * zones, convention/rest/default text, effective return before
// effect arrow, via, explicit empty effect row, policies and failure source.

// collect_stmts -> Statements.jet:12 semindex_collect_stmts. collect_loop_label_def
// -> Statements.jet:16 semindex_collect_loop_label_def. collect_loop_label_ref ->
// Statements.jet:23–29 semindex_loop_label_span and
// semindex_collect_loop_label_ref; reference length is UTF-8 bytes, not scalars.
// collect_stmt -> Statements.jet:31–133 semindex_collect_stmt. Every statement arm
// shares structural slots; runtime/comptime switch arm boundaries, loop labels,
// range/stride/afterthought, unsafe bypasses and context fields retain their
// original traversal order. Break/Continue have no reference payload.
// collect_lvalue -> Statements.jet:135 semindex_collect_lvalue. collect_binding ->
// Statements.jet:149 semindex_collect_binding. Destructured initializer precedes
// named definitions; only inferred annotations get inlays. collect_call_inlay_hints
// -> Statements.jet:170 semindex_collect_call_inlay_hints. Uses a binder-slot map;
// explicit/missing/empty labels and repeated tails skip.

// collect_expr -> Expressions.jet:89–319 semindex_collect_expr. Preserves ghost
// copies, arithmetic facts, calls/member references, explicit drop reason, all
// operand/list/map/tuple/type/fallback slots, lambda/if binding traversal,
// checked origin sentinel AND original source bytes, and all literal leaf arms.
// Canonical optional-call projection at Expressions.jet:68–87 represents Rust's
// CallValue/OptField shape through the same node/slot/reference producers.
// format_arithmetic_hover -> Expressions.jet:31 semindex_format_arithmetic_hover.
// collect_expr_stmt -> Expressions.jet:323 semindex_collect_expr_stmt; only Expr
// and DeferClose recurse, not unrelated statement forms.

// No inline original tests occur in 1776–3654. Behavioral normalization and
// arithmetic-render controls are paired in Tests/SemIndex/Build02.jet.
// No new module imports/manifest hunk: canonical Structure, Items, ItemFacts,
// Statements and Expressions already contain and call every mapped declaration.
// #4494/#4483/#4499/#4409: no native/target/composite-key/IO primitive in this
// window; typed AST/name-ledger producer integration remains canonical-owned.
